===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|originally}} One who is [[name]]d after another or for whom another is named.
#: {{syn|en|eponym}}
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|year=2018|author=James Lambert|title=Setting the Record Straight: An In-depth Examination of ''Hobson-Jobson''|journal=International Journal of Lexicography|volume=31|issue=4|doi=https://doi.org/10.1093/ijl/ecy010|page=493|text=It is the only citation from 1902, and was clearly added to the manuscript at a late stage, being only one of two examples of the dictionary’s '''namesake''' actually discovered by Crooke.}}
# {{lb|en|by extension}} A [[ship]] or a [[building]] that is named after someone or something.
# A person with the same name as another.

